ays Lycaon. He fed Zeus human flesh and was turned into a wolf as punishment.It might need a little extra work to do but Werewolfs could be the descendants of Lycaon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:05:22-07:00","id":294141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badger King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=294076#post294076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for other possible origin myths there's always Lycaon. He fed Zeus human flesh and was turned into a wolf as punishment.It might need a little extra work to do but Werewolfs could be the descendants of Lycaon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, in fact, an alternative mythology in <i>Blasphemies</i> that evokes that particular legend - &quot;Curse of the Werewolf,&quot; (pages 21-23) best kept by the Lodge of Arkadia (pages 74-76 of the same book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T00:27:45-07:00","id":294594,"title":"","content":"And if memory serves, in Blasphemies there is also a myth that werewolves are the adopted kids of Mama Wolf who nursed them, a celtic inspired story of cursed demigods, and a myth that is Amerindian inspired about wolves who decided that having thumbs would be awesome, am I missing any?<br /> <br /> On rpgnet I suggested a gnostic origin story based on the Jail of Night hack for owod as a potential nwod myth , which is humanity is comprised of fallen gods and werewolves are the result of some of those fallen gods being implanted into wolf bodies by mistake, Father Wolf could be the werewolf who inspired the werewolves to take care of the material world and spiritual world as acts of contrition, so the Pure would be the werewolves who never forgot that they are fallen gods but feel free to continue to act like the spoiled divine brats humanity supposedly used to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:29:17-07:00","id":297508,"title":"","content":"I can't recall what they called them, but in Demon the Fallen, Demons believed that werewolves were the product of Angels mating with animals, similar to the Nephilim. I'll have to look through my books to find where it is because I can't remember of hand. It could even come from the fiction trilogy.<br /> <br /> Still an interesting alternate myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:32:56-07:00","id":297511,"title":"","content":"I read an article at one of Polish sites that the use of lunar calendar in early Hebrew culture could indicate a link between YHWH and Moon. Maybe Werewolves through early Abrahamic lens are linked to YHWH somehow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:59:02-07:00","id":297576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=297511#post297511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read an article at one of Polish sites that the use of lunar calendar in early Hebrew culture could indicate a link between YHWH and Moon. Maybe Werewolves through early Abrahamic lens are linked to YHWH somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange I didn't hear about this little folklore of our nation. Link me to page, I will gladly translate it for the Onyx Path forums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T22:17:57-07:00","id":297814,"title":"","content":"I would translate it myself probably, but I await two major translation requests from my workplace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strange I didn't hear about this little folklore of our nation. Link me to page, I will gladly translate it for the Onyx Path forums. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.racjonalista.pl/kk.php/s,2679/q,Lunarne.aspekty.Judaizmu\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.racjonalista.pl/kk.php/s,...pekty.Judaizmu</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T22:36:20-07:00","id":297842,"title":"","content":"If one wants to tie lycanthropy to christianity, one only has to look at myths like the Livonian werewolf.<br /> <br /> Theis(s) was put on trial for heresy, his defense was that he was one of God's chosen werewolves who ventured into Hell to fight the Devil and his witches to ensure a good harvest.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of surprised that &quot;god' hounds&quot; hasn't been used more in roleplaying games, although I wouldn't be surprised if that legend had a small part inspiring the &quot;shamanistic warrior protecting the earth&quot; that wod did in both incarnations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T00:35:30-07:00","id":297913,"title":"","content":"Or this guy, who went the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Stumpp\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6e/Peter_Stump_execution.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Stumpp\" target=\"_blank\"> Peter Stumpp - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Stumpp\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Stumpp </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-31-2014, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:37:07-07:00","id":298027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm kind of surprised that &quot;god' hounds&quot; hasn't been used more in roleplaying games, although I wouldn't be surprised if that legend had a small part inspiring the &quot;shamanistic warrior protecting the earth&quot; that wod did in both incarnations. </div> </div> </div>W20 had objectively best camp in form of werewolf 'nuns' (as in modern era majority of their followers were secular Catholics). I'm inclined to port them to 2ed, since they are my favorite thing in the previous line. With adding male werewolves in the mix.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T11:23:54-07:00","id":298314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298027#post298027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 had objectively best camp in form of werewolf 'nuns' (as in modern era majority of their followers were secular Catholics). I'm inclined to port them to 2ed, since they are my favorite thing in the previous line. With adding male werewolves in the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spin-off lodge of Salvation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T13:52:13-07:00","id":298398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=272931#post272931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, Romulus could be used to depict the Forsaken, and Remus the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this one's from a while ago, but the Romulus/Remus connection just made me flash back to something John Finnemore wrote:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Phone ringing)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cHello, Rome HQ, working on a Rome for tomorrow.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cHello Romulus, is that you?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cOh hi mum, are you okay?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cYes I\u2019m fine, how are you?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cAh pretty busy, you know, with Rome\u2026 I mean it\u2019s fairly well established now but what we\u2019re finding is that\u2019s when the real work begins.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cThat\u2019s wonderful, we\u2019re all so proud of you Romulus, especially your brother.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cRemus? I don\u2019t think so.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cOf course he is, it\u2019s just hard for him you know, with Rome such a succes. He always feels like he\u2019s in your shadow. In fact, that\u2019s what I\u2019m calling about. I want you to give Remus a hand.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cA hand with what?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cYou know what.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cOh mum\u2026 is this about Reme?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cHe showed me the plans for it again yesterday, it\u2019s a really good idea for a city. He just needs a little leg up.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cMum, Reme is never going to happen. It\u2019s a fantasy.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cWell, not without some help, no.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cNot under any circumstances. If he wanted a city, he should\u2019ve started when I did. He was too busy bumming around Elyria, playing his lute. I\u2019m sorry but it\u2019s too late now, Rome wasn\u2019t build\u2026-\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cYes, yes, so you always say. Look, I\u2019m not asking you to do it for him, all I\u2019m asking is for you to have a word in a few ears.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cBut mum it\u2019s a terrible idea for a city! I mean, huge parts of it are just ripped off from Rome anyway, and the bits he\u2019s changed he\u2019s made worse. It\u2019s not going to be a better city because it\u2019s build on eight hills. It\u2019s not how it works.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cWell then help him. Show him where he\u2019s gone wrong.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cHe won\u2019t listen to me, he thinks I\u2019m an evil corporate sell out, just because I\u2019ve put in prisons and banks. I\u2019m sorry but try running a city without them. If you actually want to make a city work you\u2019ve got to serve your inhabitants. When in Rome\u2026-\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cYes, I know. You won\u2019t help him at all?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cOh don\u2019t make it sound like that mum, I would help but it\u2019ll never work! If only because all the infrastructure has been set up for Rome now. There\u2019s no room for Reme.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cWhy not?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cWell for a start, all roads lead to-\u2026\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cI see! Well Rommy, I\u2019ve listened to your objections and I do understand but I\u2019m putting my foot down. I want you to do whatever you need to do to help your brother make Reme happen. Do I make myself clear?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cWhy should I?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cBecause I\u2019m your mother.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cAnd if I don\u2019t?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cWell\u2026 then I\u2019ll just have to tear you to pieces with my mighty she wolf jaws! Grrrrrrr!!!\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T15:08:39-07:00","id":298483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298398#post298398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rome: \u201cAnd if I don\u2019t?\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother: \u201cWell\u2026 then I\u2019ll just have to tear you to pieces with my mighty she wolf jaws! Grrrrrrr!!!\u201d</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very curious how would Luna then interfere in this situation:&quot;Love, stop this non-sence, Romulus had better plan in the first place. It's Remus problem&quot;, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T16:06:43-07:00","id":298515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=297814#post297814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(About Hebrew and Moon connection)<br /> <br /> I would translate it myself probably, but I await two major translation requests from my workplace.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.racjonalista.pl/kk.php/s,2679/q,Lunarne.aspekty.Judaizmu\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.racjonalista.pl/kk.php/s,...pekty.Judaizmu</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, idea is this - early Hebrew there is odd correlation of they calendar, 28 day month ( 4 times 7 days week ) and New Moon. First Shabbat of the year comes in the New Moon, seventh is most sacred of them all, worshiped very extensively in early Old Testament. At the beginning of books day starts at the dawn ( solar cult ), but later, start of the Shabbat is at the seventh day's dusk ( lunar cult ). In the middle of Old Testament there is mentioned purge in Israel, negating worship of other gods in it. From then on only YHWH is mentioned - but clues from earlier cult were left, and calendar or Shabbat practices remained, pointing on that probably Moon cult was absorbed in to Tetragrammaton itself.<br /> <br /> My take on this idea of Jewish werewolves myth based on it would be this...<br /> <br /> <b>Unholy Sons</b><br /> <br /> <br /> On the beginning was a Word. And Word was a World. The Father created with the Word whole Creation. And it was good. He later created humans in Paradise and gave them free will. But Eve, first women, was tempted by the Snake to obtain the apple from Tree of Knowledge. And they needed to be banished from the Paradise.<br /> <br /> But Father weren\u2019t only having righteous face of the Sun. He was forgiving as the Moon. He couldn\u2019t lifted his own decree, because he knew it was right - humans weren\u2019t suppose to return to Paradise any more. But he also couldn\u2019t left Adam and Eve, and the kind alone in the world. He needed to defend them, and Paradise against them.<br /> <br /> As the Moon, he appeared to the most dangerous of Paradise animal and come to make with it the race of guardians. The Father Moon conceived with Mother Wolf new kind - half man, half wolves. Not pure as humans, but needed to protect them and the world from the man. As sons and daughters of so foul creature as Wolf, they could do what need to be done - even go to the Hell itself, if the need rose.<br /> <br /> But the Wolf Mother wanted more and more of her half human children to behave like a wolves, forsaking they sacred duty from the Father. Then he come to them and told what need to be done. And so they killed they Mother under his command, like Isaac was ready to sacrifice his son.<br /> This is who we are - we are His children, with duty to him and respect to our Mother memory. We didn\u2019t destroyed the Paradise, but were made to guard it. And now we atone for our sins in the eyes of Father.<br /> <br /> So what do you think about this story? It\u2019s only first draft, I will make it more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T04:41:05-07:00","id":298850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298027#post298027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 had objectively best camp in form of werewolf 'nuns' (as in modern era majority of their followers were secular Catholics). I'm inclined to port them to 2ed, since they are my favorite thing in the previous line. With adding male werewolves in the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shouldn't be hard in concept, since somewhere (blood of the wolf?) it mentions that a lot of the forsaken retain their human religion. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298515#post298515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you think about this story? It\u2019s only first draft, I will make it more later.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well first of all, I'd get rid of the apple reference, the fruit of the tree of knowledge of good and evil being an apple is a pun based on the language of the church, latin. So I don't think the werewolves would appreciate that joke and I'm sure the pun doesn't work in either Hebrew or Enochian or whatever you'd have the first tongue be based on here. <br /> <br /> And where exactly is Eden supposed to be in this? A place on earth? Because in that case humanity probably bulldozed it to make a starbucks parking lot. The shadow? Humans need more protection from the shadow than vice versa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-01-2014, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T04:57:13-07:00","id":298857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shouldn't be hard in concept, since somewhere (blood of the wolf?) it mentions that a lot of the forsaken retain their human religion. </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah, then my mind is set on porting them, I will just wait for 2ed to be available.<br /> <br /> Lancea Et Sanctum fashions themselves as an ancient order of monsters serving the God? How cute. There were things lurking in the shadows long before Rome was even established. Sanctfied think of themselves as God's predators preying on mortal sheep. They should be careful lest they alert His shepherd hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-01-2014, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T09:55:19-07:00","id":299023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=298850#post298850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where exactly is Eden supposed to be in this? A place on earth? Because in that case humanity probably bulldozed it to make a starbucks parking lot. The shadow? Humans need more protection from the shadow than vice versa</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking the Eden was Pangea part of the world - where the Shadow and Material being one. With this myth, Jewish Uratha could search it once more - to return to the Paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T11:34:30-07:00","id":299116,"title":"","content":"Probably they cannot gain Essence from eating humans because I guess God would forbid them to do so. All hail kosher diet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T23:44:21-07:00","id":299760,"title":"","content":"Hmm, yeah keeping kosher on a cannibal diet is a sticky subject, perhaps they gain essence by following their virtue (bone)? Or regenerate essence if they don't violate certain religious laws kind of like mages with their oblations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:56:29-08:00","id":299884,"title":"","content":"That could be a sort of a covenant with God, for adhering to their duties they are blessed by their patron in a certain way, possibly in ways that you suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T03:39:14-08:00","id":299895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=299116#post299116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably they cannot gain Essence from eating humans because I guess God would forbid them to do so. All hail kosher diet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have thought the opposite - they <i>can </i>gain Essence from eating humans, because you need the Devil playing the role of the tempter after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T03:50:52-08:00","id":299898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would have thought the opposite - they can gain Essence from eating humans, because you need the Devil playing the role of the tempter after all... </div> </div> </div>That's not congruent with my concept, so not in my case. Partly because it feels like Lancea Et Sanctum 2: Electric Boogaloo, and because I envision them in more like Forsaken's role to &quot;police the neighborhood&quot; but in more specific way. The tempter's role does not fit in my opinion. They probably should get free pass to not suffer the witch to live if by a witch we mean 'heathens' who summon spirits against the commandment of God to do not so. That could probably also involve summoning of ghosts since Saul contacting a witch from Endor to summon Samuel (I think) was not exactly applauded.<br /> <br /> On another hand there are tales of King Solomon binding spirits and demons so there is a degree of hipocrisy.<br /> <br /> PS. Feel free to do as you like, since that's only my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-02-2014, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T14:06:42-08:00","id":300437,"title":"","content":"I don't think he meant it as something that they regularly did, i.e. playing God's monster, but something that is forbidden, but that they can be tempted with. Look at it this way, they are low on Essence, but need to save people. IF they just... ate one body, they could save more people. What is one life compared to 5, 10, 20 people? It's a temptation, a source of drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T14:49:32-08:00","id":300482,"title":"","content":"Catholicism, at least, already has its ritual eating of flesh. Incorporating the Eucharist into a Uratha rite wouldn't be that big a leap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T01:36:48-08:00","id":300873,"title":"","content":"^That's not exactly same thing, as eating humans and eating God could be considered a different thing.<br /> <br /> But I don't worry about that, since I build my lodge as primarily Jewish in the origins anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:34:22-08:00","id":302779,"title":"","content":"This story is true.<br /> <br /> There was a time before all this. Something more primal, more raw. Some would call it purer, or better for it, but that's a lie. Taking away cell phones and microwaves doesn't make something morally better. This was a savage time, of ever-changing horrors you can scarcely imagine. Luna hung high over the Earth day and night, casting not just her light, but her power over the world. Things changed, warped, mutated constantly. The line between spirit and man shifted perpetually, sometimes breaking altogether. Too often. More often than Father Wolf would like.<br /> <br /> The self-styled guardian of borders, Father Wolf's job of guarding the physical from the ephemeral and vice-versa was very nearly impossible under Luna's tyranny. Father Wolf was not meant to be an intelligent thing. He was the Hunter, and wanted little more than to hunt those that would break the law. When the law becomes as immutable as everything else, though, when the world changes at the whims of a mad tyrant-queen with the power to go entirely unopposed, creativity was needed. He had learned cunning, but to protect the borders, to hold his post, he needed more.<br /> <br /> Legends spoke of a city, somewhere in this changing world, a place where the few enlightened among mankind gathered and called down power of their own, a port in the neverending storm. A watchtower. Knowing this was the ally he needed to wage war with the moon, Father Wolf traveled to this city's walls, and waited. His children, the Firstborn, he knew, would stand watch over Luna's madness. They couldn't hold the fort forever, and so on the fifth day, when the Awakened City had still not allowed him entry, Father Wolf laid siege upon the walls, roaring his demand to speak with those who would call themselves gods. In that moment, the city was his prey. He was the Wolf. He would not, could not be denied.<br /> <br /> The Awakened City shattered. Luna's influence poured in, and the single watchtower in an ocean of ever-changing madness fell. Finally, one of the Mages of the city called out to Father Wolf. &quot;Why did you do this,&quot; she cried! &quot;Do you know what you have done?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It isn't the Wolf's place to care about his prey.&quot; Father Wolf responded. He told them of his unique problem, The Mages may have felt pity, if Father Wolf had not damned them. It would be a slow decline, but with the walls that protected the Awakened City from Luna the Tyrant broken, the Mages would always carry something of her hatred, and that hatred would twist their magics into strange shapes that brought forth the darkest places the world had to offer.<br /> <br /> Father Wolf was not the only one who knew cunning. The mages plotted, and gave the spirit wolfsbane in the guise of an olive branch.<br /> <br /> There was one way to do away with Luna the Tyrant, they told Father Wolf. They would use the last of their power to construct a machine to drain Luna's godly might, make her no more powerful than Father Wolf, who would consume her. A new Luna would be born, for that was her nature, but it would be a weaker, tamer Luna.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you could do such a thing,&quot; Father Wolf asked, &quot;Why had you not done it already?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mages answered. &quot;Because no spirit capable of killing the weakened Tyrant was available to us. And it will cost you your life.&quot; This was their revenge. They would give Father Wolf what he wanted, and would make the Fallen World to come a more habitable place in the absence of their paradise. At the same time, it would kill he who damned them. After another five days and another five nights, he accepted. He saw no other path to victory in the war he had started against Luna.<br /> <br /> The Mages built their God-Machine, and Father Wolf returned to his children to find them weakened and broken. He told them of the Mages, and what they had come up with.<br /> <br /> Three of his children, those most wounded by his absence, were furious. Dire Wolf, Rabid Wolf, and Silver Wolf swore that they would never give up the war, and if Father Wolf became one with the Moon, then he would become their enemy.This was acceptable to Father Wolf. The remaining Firstborn agreed to forsake their hatred, if it meant peace, a world they could protect effectively.<br /> <br /> The Mages made their play. Luna was aware of what they intended, but was unable to stop them, as even she could not control her changes, and could not retain her mind long enough to counterattack. The Mages' God-Machine worked as it was meant to, and Luna was mortally wounded. She could no longer force her changing nature upon the world, and her light could only show at night, a dim reflection of what she once was.<br /> <br /> The machine poured its power into Father Wolf, and with his dying breath, gifted this power to his children, and their children, and so forth. Those who descended from the Firstborn were given the power of the Moon, to change shape and walk between the worlds of spirit and man, which were now solidly divided Only the Forsaken, who gave up their hatred for the Moon, were able to use her full might, and it is said that Luna the Broken shows favor to them through her Gifts. The Lunes, spirit memories of Luna the Tyrant, still exist though, aiding and tormenting the Forsaken in equal measure. While they may guide the Forsaken when it aids their twisted agenda, taking one as a totem would surely invite the Tyrant's wrath back into the world.<br /> <br /> This is how it is. The Forsaken carry on their Father's legacy of stewardship and protection, and the Pure carry on their Father's legacy of war against Luna.<br /> <br /> This is how it will always be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T04:45:03-08:00","id":303188,"title":"","content":"That last story could turn on the legend of Coyolxauhqui.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:54:25-08:00","id":303335,"title":"","content":"Blah, blah, mages did everything, blah, blah.<br /> <br /> I dearly, dearly hope the above isn't given any kind of official weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T09:10:54-08:00","id":303344,"title":"","content":"Mages don't really DO anything, they just dig up who did, then claim them as one of their own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T09:29:08-08:00","id":303351,"title":"","content":"While I wouldn't like it as some sort of official offering, it makes perfect sense within the context of this thread, being an alternative werewolf myth in the form of werewolf myth.<br /> <br /> We Werewolf fans are touchy (defensive, even) about Mage stuff getting into our setting. I'm apparently wrong about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  No need to be a jerkass. 11-05-2014, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T10:48:42-08:00","id":303400,"title":"","content":"I'm touchy about mage getting into any setting.... But it was a well written myth, and did a good job explaining a lot of modern phenomena in the WoD. Also, it set the gratifying precedent of werewolves beating up mages until they get they the bizarre magics they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T15:17:55-08:00","id":303772,"title":"","content":"Just so we're clear that was not the slightest bit official, I just wanted to write something cool. Besides that, like Seraph said, the point of putting Mages in the story was to have werewolves beat them up to get what they want.<br /> <br /> I can take the post down if it's that upsetting. @_@ I didn't want to make anyone mad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T15:23:33-08:00","id":303779,"title":"","content":"No, no keep it up! I love that. (I, however, run a crossover setting so that is right up my alley) I actually like it so much I'm adapting it for my WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:12:41-08:00","id":303834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303335#post303335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blah, blah, mages did everything, blah, blah.<br /> <br /> I dearly, dearly hope the above isn't given any kind of official weight.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303351#post303351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it would be awful if it was some sort of official offering, it makes perfect sense within the context of this thread, being an alternative werewolf myth in the form of werewolf myth.<br /> <br /> We Werewolf fans are touchy (defensive, even) about Mage stuff getting into our setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, given that it's just a myth that no werewolf can actually verify, and is presented as one of those heretical tales you might hear, it wouldn't hurt to show a little more respect. A simple &quot;I'm not a big fan of Mage stuff mixing with my Werewolf, but it's an interesting idea&quot; or &quot;I wouldn't personally use it, because I don't like Mage getting into my Werewolf&quot; would be a lot kinder than dismissive snark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:19:00-08:00","id":303838,"title":"","content":"The goal was to write an alternate myth. I thought about what a werewolf might come up with to explain the universe if he didn't buy into the Father Wolf story as presented. If he's met Mages and knows about their history, it wouldn't be a huge leap of logic to link these two vaguely-defined before times.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is just there because I like the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> That's all I was trying to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T16:30:44-08:00","id":303848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303335#post303335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blah, blah, mages did everything, blah, blah.<br /> <br /> I dearly, dearly hope the above isn't given any kind of official weight.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303344#post303344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't really DO anything, they just dig up who did, then claim them as one of their own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would be fucking fantastic if the Werewolf boards did not see fit to pick up the banner of the old Changeling boards in producing vast stinking clouds of disproportionate whining backlash against the gameline whose PR has been tainted by a handful of readers who think it's cute to claim the supernatural group concerned with trying to understand everything already understands everything. It's long passed the point of being even darkly and bitterly amusing how much more concerned people get about Mage &quot;taking over&quot; other lines than over even claims of such actually occurring - now it's just kind of disgusting.<br /> <br /> It would be just super if the forumgoers could at least maintain the basic decorum requisite for not driving writers of any stripe away from engaging with the material in a public fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:27:02-08:00","id":303921,"title":"","content":"I heartily second that, Satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T18:05:40-08:00","id":303940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303834#post303834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple &quot;I'm not a big fan of Mage stuff mixing with my Werewolf, but it's an interesting idea&quot; or &quot;I wouldn't personally use it, because I don't like Mage getting into my Werewolf&quot; would be a lot kinder than dismissive snark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured the Like button would get the more positive 'I like it' across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T18:11:26-08:00","id":303943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303351#post303351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it would be awful if it was some sort of official offering, it makes perfect sense within the context of this thread, being an alternative werewolf myth in the form of werewolf myth.<br /> <br /> We Werewolf fans are touchy (defensive, even) about Mage stuff getting into our setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, don't put words in my mouth, eh? Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303834#post303834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, given that it's just a myth that no werewolf can actually verify, and is presented as one of those heretical tales you might hear, it wouldn't hurt to show a little more respect. A simple &quot;I'm not a big fan of Mage stuff mixing with my Werewolf, but it's an interesting idea&quot; or &quot;I wouldn't personally use it, because I don't like Mage getting into my Werewolf&quot; would be a lot kinder than dismissive snark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I think my reply fully captured the essence of the submission above. But we can agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303848#post303848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be fucking fantastic if the Werewolf boards did not see fit to pick up the banner of the old Changeling boards in producing vast stinking clouds of disproportionate whining backlash against the gameline whose PR has been tainted by a handful of readers who think it's cute to claim the supernatural group concerned with trying to understand everything already understands everything. It's long passed the point of being even darkly and bitterly amusing how much more concerned people get about Mage &quot;taking over&quot; other lines than over even claims of such actually occurring - now it's just kind of disgusting.<br /> <br /> It would be just super if the forumgoers could at least maintain the basic decorum requisite for not driving writers of any stripe away from engaging with the material in a public fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the risks of the job isn't it? Criticism. Clich\u00e9s, specially are a peeve of mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303838#post303838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal was to write an alternate myth. I thought about what a werewolf might come up with to explain the universe if he didn't buy into the Father Wolf story as presented. If he's met Mages and knows about their history, it wouldn't be a huge leap of logic to link these two vaguely-defined before times.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is just there because I like the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> That's all I was trying to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, by all means, keep it posted. If you need a positive insight? pick an interlocutor. Decide from which side the story is being told and make it unmistakably clear for the reader, and if you're going to name drop things like Atlantis, Urfarah, and the God Machine? do create an actual myth in terms of verbiage, so that one can actually picture said time and place. Give examples of said 'madness', for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T18:23:37-08:00","id":303972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303943#post303943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I think my reply fully captured the essence of the submission above. But we can agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we can't agree to disagree. Your reply touched absolutely nothing and clarified nothing. It was insulting for the sake of being insulting and had absolutely no critical value in the slightest. I'm reporting you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303943#post303943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the risks of the job isn't it? Criticism. Clich\u00e9s, specially are a peeve of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, considering that the story is a unique creation myth, I'd be curious to know how it's in any way a cliche. But since you've no interest in any kind of reasonable critical discussion and have demonstrated both unwillingness and inability to actually engage, it's not like you'd explain anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T19:12:34-08:00","id":303999,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">There is a line between criticism and insult that is starting to be crossed here, and by more than one poster. If you don't like an alternative myth presented here, don't respond to it. <br /> <br /> Now let's cease the personal attacks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:40:24-08:00","id":304115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=303848#post303848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be fucking fantastic if the Werewolf boards did not see fit to pick up the banner of the old Changeling boards in producing vast stinking clouds of disproportionate whining backlash against the gameline whose PR has been tainted by a handful of readers who think it's cute to claim the supernatural group concerned with trying to understand everything already understands everything. It's long passed the point of being even darkly and bitterly amusing how much more concerned people get about Mage &quot;taking over&quot; other lines than over even claims of such actually occurring - now it's just kind of disgusting.<br /> <br /> It would be just super if the forumgoers could at least maintain the basic decorum requisite for not driving writers of any stripe away from engaging with the material in a public fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, pal. I'm so far out of the loop with WoD 2.0, I'll just go back to reading my X20 stuff and stay out of the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:31:46-08:00","id":304148,"title":"","content":"Ah, don't do that! It's always good to see you here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T22:47:34-08:00","id":304212,"title":"","content":"We are the Forsaken, for we refused the flesh of our flesh. We are Forsaken, for we did not come to our Father's aid. When the world was new, when spirit and flesh were the same Great Wolf and his pack hunted. Born of Grandfather Sky and Grandmother Earth, the First Pack could not be out done, when they hunted together. Great Wolf, first born of the First Pack, knew no equal even among the other 8 of his pack. His might was such that even together now two members of the pack could out-hunt him, nor could they overpower him. The world was wild and savage, and the pack never lacked prey to hunt.<br /> <br /> Centuries passed, and the First Pack hunted across them. In those years of savage grace the Pack met the many spirits-in-flesh, but none more beautiful than our Mother Moon. Great Wolf courted her and sang love songs to her, but he was not the only one who desired her. Rabid Wolf (then called Spirit Wolf), Silver Wolf and Dire Wolf each sought to earn her affections in their own way. Spirit Wolf showed Moon many of the things he had learned from other spirits, working magics both strange and terrific. Yet, for all his wonders, she spurned Spirit Wolf. Silver Wolf attempted to seduce Moon with his perfect coat and ideal features. No matter how smooth his words or beautiful his coat, Moon still rejected him. Dire Wolf sung passionate songs and brought Moon the hides of his most daring kills. Despite the lavish gifts and beautiful songs, Moon denied Dire Wolf for her heart belonged to another.<br /> <br /> Each Wolf sang their sorrows in the dark places of the savage world, and each heard the other. They hurt and it only grew worse when they heard that Great Wolf's love song to Moon. They had been spurned for the Alpha, and their love for Moon became hate for Great Wolf. It was decided that they would lure Great Wolf to the darkest place they could find and destroy their rival. Spirit Wolf, in a righteous fury, called upon every trick and talent the spirits had showed him and would lead Great Wolf astray. Silver Wolf with simmering hate would betray Great Wolf when he needed it most. Dire wolf, his heart cold, would wait and in the darkest place, he would kill Great Wolf.<br /> <br /> While Great Wolf was with Moon, Rabid Wolf's spirit tricks drew them away. Silver Wolf broke in to Great Wolf's dalliance, and showed him to the dark path. Once they were in the deepest shadows, Dire Wolf and Silver Wolf attacked. However, Great Wolf was stronger than any two of the Pack, but he was not untouchable. He howled, begging for help from the Pack, but they were too far away to hear. Rabid Wolf lead the Pack further and further out, his rage twisting his features. In the Dark, those spirits whom Great Wolf had hunted but could not kill crawled from the shadows and joined in the killing.<br /> <br /> Not bad for a rough draft of an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T02:40:25-08:00","id":304328,"title":"","content":"Also, it turns the usual tale upside down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T03:30:31-08:00","id":304388,"title":"","content":"I so far avoided crossing what I make for Forsaken with Mage. Only Celestines involved with origins of Urathra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T12:06:50-08:00","id":371287,"title":"","content":"I'm refreshing a bit topic of Roman Uratha with this beautiful graphics...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc04.deviantart.net/fs71/i/2012/150/e/c/matriarchy_by_classic_syndrome-d51oqds.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So Mother ( Capitoline ) Wolf, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T12:30:43-08