date":"2015-01-15T13:07:23-08:00","id":371379,"title":"","content":"*Looks at the title.*<br /> <br /> Instead of the whole &quot;You were never human to begin with&quot; trope, it would be far more interesting to have Lupines to have an infection/impressment into the folds. You just so happened to be bitten by a wolf while it wasin Death Rage and survived only to have to deal with finding yourself getting a little fuzzy you're self.<br /> <br /> Or you simply attracted the eyes of the insane moon spirit and she simply decided that genetics be damned, you're gonna howl at the moon for the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> Not to say that doesn't already happen but I've always thought about playing with the other parts of the Werewolf myth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:15:41-08:00","id":371389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=371379#post371379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks at the title.*<br /> <br /> Instead of the whole &quot;You were never human to begin with&quot; trope, it would be far more interesting to have Lupines to have an infection/impressment into the folds. You just so happened to be bitten by a wolf while it wasin Death Rage and survived only to have to deal with finding yourself getting a little fuzzy you're self.<br /> <br /> Or you simply attracted the eyes of the insane moon spirit and she simply decided that genetics be damned, you're gonna howl at the moon for the rest of your life.<br /> <br /> Not to say that doesn't already happen but I've always thought about playing with the other parts of the Werewolf myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was spoilered that this things can lead to become Wolf Blooded in 2ed <b>Werewolf</b>. Now, when we will see it in book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:25:03-08:00","id":371393,"title":"","content":"I think in one of the Werewolf storyteller's guides they had the rules outlined to play one of the Cursed. They also mentioned Wild Children, or Jackals (if you decide the Uratha exist and know of them), and their whole shtick feels very Maeljin-rooted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:55:42-08:00","id":408526,"title":"","content":"Well, D&amp;D 3.5 got away with all male creator gods except for one Halfling goddess who had to pinch bits of other races because she wasn't capable of birthing a race on her own (being female, I guess, is a handicap to birthing a race) so two female goddesses making a child makes at least as much sense. At the very least, neither the male nor the female gods are assumed to have wombs and willies so really the whole gendering of deities would theoretically be more about masculine and feminine principles than biological anatomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}